# What must never enter the build context.
#
# There was no ignore file at all, and it cost two things.
#
# CORRECTNESS. The Containerfile does `COPY apps/web/ ./` after running
# `pnpm install` inside the image. With node_modules in the context, the
# host's macOS/arm64 binaries land on top of the container's linux/arm64
# install and the build dies on:
#
#     Cannot find module @rollup/rollup-linux-arm64-gnu
#
# which reads like a dependency bug and is really a copy order problem.
#
# SIZE. The context was 2.3 GB, of which 1.7 GB is apps/api/.venv (it
# contains torch) and 291 MB is node_modules — all of it re-resolved inside
# the image anyway.

# --- dependency trees: always rebuilt inside the image --------------------
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# --- build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# apps/api/static is the EXCEPTION: the runtime stage copies the SPA build
# from the spa-builder stage, not from the host, so the host copy is dead
# weight in the context.
apps/web/dist/
apps/api/static/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- local state, never shipped -------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
backups/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# --- secrets: belt and braces --------------------------------------------
# Config comes from the environment and from settings overrides written
# through the admin UI. Nothing resembling a credential should be reachable
# from a build.
.env
.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
